  "Question": "The sum of two numbers is \\(10;\\) their product is \\(20.\\) The sum of their reciprocals is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(\\dfrac1{10}\\)",
    "B": "\\(\\dfrac12\\)",
    "C": "\\(1\\)",
    "D": "\\(2\\)",
    "E": "\\(4\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Let the numbers be \\(u\\) and \\(v\\). Since \\(uv=20\\ne0\\), both reciprocals are defined. Combining them over the common denominator \\(uv\\) uses exactly the two quantities we know:\n\\[\n\\frac1u+\\frac1v=\\frac{u+v}{uv}=\\frac{10}{20}=\\frac12.\n\\]\nThus the answer is \\(\\boxed{\\frac12}\\), choice \\(\\boxed{\\text{B}}\\).",
